---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PolicyContact from "../components/PolicyContact.astro";
import { LEGAL_HOLDER } from "../data/site";
---

<Layout
  title="The Bead Reserve : Accessibility"
  description="The accessibility statement for The Bead Reserve's website: conformance status, known limitations, and how to report a barrier."
>
  <main>
    <article class="policy bracket-frame">
      <h1>Accessibility</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This is the accessibility statement of The Bead Reserve, issued by
          {LEGAL_HOLDER} for this site.
        </p>

        <h2>Conformance status</h2>
        <p>
          The
          <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/"
            >Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG)</a
          >
          define requirements for making web content accessible to people with
          disabilities. This site is partially conformant with WCAG 2.2 Level
          AA. Partially conformant means that some parts of the content do not
          fully conform to the standard.
        </p>

        <h2>Feedback</h2>
        <p>
          Report an accessibility barrier on this site through any of these.
        </p>
        <PolicyContact />

        <h2>Technical specifications</h2>
        <p>
          The site is HTML and CSS. JavaScript runs the reserve monitor and the
          theme toggle. Without JavaScript, the monitor remains on its sealed
          placeholder.
        </p>

        <h2>Known limitations</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            The reserve monitor is a black screen in both themes. This is
            deliberate. Its state is also given in text, in the badge and the
            captions around the screen. The camera frame carries alt text.
          </li>
          <li>
            The reserve seal turns over on hover or keyboard focus to show its
            reverse. This is deliberate. The seal's label states both faces in
            text, so nothing is lost if the turn is not seen.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>Report any issue not listed here.</p>

        <h2>Assessment approach</h2>
        <p>
          {LEGAL_HOLDER} assessed this site by self-evaluation. Every change to
          the site also runs automated checks. axe-core tests every page against
          WCAG 2.2 A and AA in both the light and dark themes. A keyboard walk
          of the home page confirms that every focus stop shows a ring.
          html-validate checks the markup of every built page.
        </p>

        <h2>Date</h2>
        <p>This statement was written on October 7, 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
